Refactor App.tsx into Context Providers in a clean, incremental, copy-pasteable way so you can actually use it, not just conceptually admire it.

Below is a clinically safe, scalable architecture that fits where PediPulse is heading.

🎯 Goal of This Refactor

Remove state + persistence + business logic from App.tsx

Avoid prop-drilling across medical features

Make future features (handover summary, exports, audits) easy

Keep medical data handling explicit and safe

🧱 Target Architecture
src/
├─ context/
│  ├─ ChildProfileContext.tsx
│  ├─ MedicalHistoryContext.tsx
│  └─ NavigationContext.tsx
├─ hooks/
│  └─ useLocalStorage.ts
├─ App.tsx
└─ main.tsx / index.tsx

1️⃣ Create a Safe useLocalStorage Hook

src/hooks/useLocalStorage.ts

import { useState, useEffect } from "react";

export function useLocalStorage<T>(key: string, initialValue: T) {
  const [value, setValue] = useState<T>(() => {
    try {
      const stored = localStorage.getItem(key);
      return stored ? JSON.parse(stored) : initialValue;
    } catch {
      return initialValue;
    }
  });

  useEffect(() => {
    try {
      localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(value));
    } catch {
      // Fail silently – never crash on persistence
    }
  }, [key, value]);

  return [value, setValue] as const;
}


✅ Protects against corrupted data
✅ Centralises persistence
✅ Critical for medical data safety

2️⃣ Navigation Context

src/context/NavigationContext.tsx

