I’ll do this in two parts:

Clinical Governance Log (Decision Rationale)

Low-Resource Setting Mode (Offline + Conservative Defaults)

Both are designed to be useful, not just “compliance theatre”.

1️⃣ Clinical Governance Log (Decision Rationale)
🎯 Purpose

Create a non-judgemental audit trail that records:

What the app suggested

Why it suggested it

What red flags were present

What mode the user was in (parent vs clinician)

Whether the app was online/offline

This protects:

Users

You (developer)

Future clinical collaborators

Importantly:
👉 This is not a legal record or medical note — it’s a decision-support rationale log.

A. Governance Log Data Model

src/clinical/governance.ts

export type GovernanceEventType =
  | "symptom_evaluation"
  | "dose_calculation"
  | "screening_result"
  | "handover_generated";

export type GovernanceEntry = {
  id: string;
  timestamp: string;
  eventType: GovernanceEventType;
  userRole: "parent" | "clinician";
  online: boolean;
  inputSummary: string;
  outputSummary: string;
  redFlags?: string[];
  disclaimerShown: boolean;
};


This deliberately:

Avoids clinical judgment language

Avoids “recommend” / “advise”

Focuses on system behaviour

B. Governance Context (Centralised + Persistent)

src/context/GovernanceContext.tsx

import { createContext, useContext } from "react";
import { useLocalStorage } from "../hooks/useLocalStorage";
import { GovernanceEntry } from "../clinical/governance";

const STORAGE_KEY = "pedipulse_governance_log";

const GovernanceContext = createContext<{
  log: GovernanceEntry[];
  addEntry: (entry: Omit<GovernanceEntry, "id" | "timestamp">) => void;
} | undefined>(undefined);

export const GovernanceProvider: React.FC<{ children: React.ReactNode }> = ({ children }) => {
  const [log, setLog] = useLocalStorage<GovernanceEntry[]>(STORAGE_KEY, []);

  const addEntry = (entry: Omit<GovernanceEntry, "id" | "timestamp">) => {
    setLog(prev => [
      {
        ...entry,
        id: crypto.randomUUID(),
        timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
      },
      ...prev
    ]);
  };

  return (
    <GovernanceContext.Provider value={{ log, addEntry }}>
      {children}
    </GovernanceContext.Provider>
  );
};

export const useGovernance = () => {
  const ctx = useContext(GovernanceContext);
  if (!ctx) throw new Error("useGovernance must be used within GovernanceProvider");
  return ctx;
};

C. Logging a Decision (Example: Symptom Checker)
const { addEntry } = useGovernance();
const online = useConnectivity();
const { role } = useRole();

addEntry({
  eventType: "symptom_evaluation",
  userRole: role,
  online,
  inputSummary: "Fever 38.5°C, age 2 months, poor feeding",
  outputSummary: "Urgent red flag surfaced: fever in infant <3 months",
  redFlags: flags.map(f => f.id),
  disclaimerShown: true
});


🔒 This creates traceability without blame.

D. Governance Log Viewer (Clinician-Only)

GovernanceLog.tsx

import { useGovernance } from "../context/GovernanceContext";

export const GovernanceLog = () => {
  const { log } = useGovernance();

  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <h1 className="text-xl font-black">Clinical Governance Log</h1>

      {log.map(entry => (
        <div key={entry.id} className="p-4 border rounded-xl text-sm">
          <p><strong>{entry.eventType}</strong> — {new Date(entry.timestamp).toLocaleString()}</p>
          <p>Role: {entry.userRole} | Online: {entry.online ? "Yes" : "No"}</p>
          <p>{entry.outputSummary}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};


This is:

Transparent

Educational

Audit-friendly

2️⃣ Low-Resource Setting Mode

(Offline + Conservative Defaults)

This is extremely aligned with your interest in low-resource pediatrics and MSF-style settings.

A. Define Low-Resource Mode

Low-resource mode enforces:

Offline-first assumptions

Conservative thresholds

Reduced complexity

Escalation bias

B. Low-Resource Context

src/context/EnvironmentContext.tsx

type EnvironmentMode = "standard" | "low-resource";

const EnvironmentContext = createContext<{
  mode: EnvironmentMode;
  setMode: (m: EnvironmentMode) => void;
} | undefined>(undefined);

export const EnvironmentProvider: React.FC<{ children: React.ReactNode }> = ({ children }) => {
  const [mode, setMode] = useLocalStorage<EnvironmentMode>(
    "pedipulse_environment",
    "standard"
  );

  return (
    <EnvironmentContext.Provider value={{ mode, setMode }}>
      {children}
    </EnvironmentContext.Provider>
  );
};

export const useEnvironment = () => {
  const ctx = useContext(EnvironmentContext);
  if (!ctx) throw new Error("useEnvironment must be used within EnvironmentProvider");
  return ctx;
};

C. Behaviour Changes in Low-Resource Mode
1️⃣ Symptom Checker

Fewer categories

Earlier escalation

Stronger wording

if (mode === "low-resource" && flags.length > 0) {
  escalationMessage =
    "If healthcare is available, seek medical assessment as soon as possible.";
}

2️⃣ Dose Calculator

Low-resource rules:

Only essential medications

Rounded doses

Larger safety margins

Max dose shown only in clinician mode

const safetyFactor = mode === "low-resource" ? 0.8 : 1;
doseMg = Math.floor(doseMg * safetyFactor / 10) * 10;

3️⃣ Red Flags

Lower thresholds:

if (mode === "low-resource" && durationDays >= 3) {
  flags.push({
    id: "early-escalation",
    message: "Early escalation recommended in low-resource settings",
    severity: "moderate"
  });
}


This mirrors WHO-style guidance: escalate earlier when support is limited.

D. UI Disclosure (Critical)

When low-resource mode is ON:

<div className="bg-amber-100 border border-amber-600 p-4 rounded-xl text-sm">
  <strong>Low-resource mode enabled</strong>
  <p>
    The app is using simplified guidance and conservative thresholds designed
    for settings with limited access to healthcare.
  </p>
</div>


This is ethical transparency.

E. Governance Logging (Tie-In)

Every governance entry already records:

Online/offline

Role

Add environment mode:

environment: mode


Now you can later say:

“This output was generated offline, in low-resource mode, using conservative thresholds.”

That is gold-standard defensibility.

